{
  "vectors": "nns/ordering",
  "version": 2,
  "spec": "nns-spec-v1 draft r27, §5.2 and §8.2",
  "description": "Canonical order is (block_number ascending, transaction hash ascending, bytewise), and tx_index is a transaction's zero-based rank in that order within its block. The rank's universe is every transaction in the block whose recipientData begins with NNS1, taken BEFORE any §7.5 discard — a discarded message still occupies its rank, and everything unprefixed is invisible to the count. Each case's transactions are authored in RESPONSE order, which deliberately never matches canonical order: a runner must rank them (the reference implementation is core's rankMessages) before reducing. txIndex on a transaction is the hand-authored expected rank; a transaction authored without txIndex must be excluded from the universe and never reduced.",
